  "notes": "Namuyi Khatho (Qiangic, Sino-Tibetan) of southwestern Sichuan, China, in the Roman orthography of Pavlík (2017) as amended by Li (2017) — the spelling the Wiktionary Namuyi corpus is written in. INPUT CONTRACT: Pavlík/Li-orthography Namuyi. CONSONANTS: a three-way retroflex/dental/alveolo-palatal split — ⟨c ch dzh sh zh⟩ = /t͡ʂ t͡ʂʰ d͡ʐ ʂ ʐ/ against ⟨ts tsh dz s z⟩ = /t͡s t͡sʰ d͡z s z/ and ⟨ky ty gy⟩ = /t͡ɕ t͡ɕ d͡ʑ/; ⟨q qh gh⟩ = /q qʰ ɢ/, ⟨hr xr⟩ = /ʁ χ/, ⟨lh⟩ = /l̥/, ⟨h⟩ = /ɦ/, ⟨ny⟩ = /ɲ/. ⟨bb db tb pb⟩ = the bilabial-trill releases /b͡ʙ d͡ʙ t͡ʙ̥ p͡ʙ̥/. A preinitial nasal assimilates: /ɴ/ before a uvular, /ŋ/ before a velar. ⟨t th⟩ palatalise to /t͡ɕ t͡ɕʰ/ before ⟨i⟩ and ⟨y⟩, and ⟨h⟩ is nasalised /ɦ̃/ before every vowel except ⟨a⟩. VOWELS: ⟨a e i o u⟩ plus ⟨ä ü⟩ = /æ y/ and the rimes ⟨ih eh uh er⟩ = /ɨ ɤ ʉ ɚ/; ⟨ih⟩ is back [ɯ] after a retroflex onset, ⟨a⟩ is backed [ɑ] after a velar or uvular and ⟨o⟩ lowered [ɔ] after a uvular. ⟨u⟩ before another vowel is the on-glide [w]; ⟨v⟩ before ⟨ih⟩ is itself the syllabic nucleus [v̩]. A word-initial vowel takes an epenthetic /ʔ/. TONE IS WRITTEN and is mapped: unmarked ⟨a⟩ = ˧, ⟨à⟩ = ˥˧, ⟨ā⟩ = ˧˩, ⟨â⟩ (⟨ä̑ ü̑⟩) = ˥, ⟨á⟩ = ˧˥ and ⟨ă⟩ = ˨, the last being Li's (2017) low toneme 21 — Module:nmy-IPA currently renders that same toneme as rising ˩˧, a notational disagreement, not a phonological one. NOT ENCODED: Namuyi has contrastive vowel NASALISATION that this orthography does not write; it is left unmapped (documented exemption) and is the main residual error against narrow transcriptions. The ⟨ă⟩ reading is load-bearing and is recorded here so it can be revisited: scored against the WikiPron snapshot, ˨ gives PER 0.1087 and ˩˧ gives 0.2211.",
